02/timeline\\\",\\n./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:3239:  \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: qpbt-stage43-magic-square-rigidity -->\\\\n### Motivation\\\\n\\\\nDischarge the external Magic Square self-testing boundary used by QPBT\\\\nsoundness. The canonical project statement is `thm:ms-rigidity` in\\\\n`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:612-652`,\\\\nmatched by `blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:224-253`. The cited\\\\nexternal source is Coladangelo--Stark, arXiv:1709.09267v2, Theorem 6.9.\\\\n\\\\nThe cited external proof obtains this as a robust linear-constraint-system\\\\nself-test using its general solution-group/stability machinery. This repository\\\\nhas no such general framework. Formalize only the finite-dimensional Magic\\\\nSquare consequence needed here; do not introduce a project-wide LCS or\\\\napproximate-representation mechanism.\\\\n\\\\n### Target\\\\n\\\\nAfter the Magic Square foundation/split packet #75, prove only the existing\\\\n`MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_ms_rigidity` in\\\\n`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems.lean`, preserving its complete public\\\\nsignature verbatim:\\\\n\\\\n- one universal `C : \\\\u211d` with `1 \\\\u2264 C`, before `\\\\u03b5` and `S`;\\\\n- every `\\\\u03b5 \\\\u2265 0` and every `S : Strategy msGame` with `1 - \\\\u03b5 \\\\u2264 S.value`;\\\\n- an `MsRigidityWitness S`;\\\\n- the Euclidean state bound;\\\\n- Alice and Bob measurement-distance bounds at zero-based variables 0/X and\\\\n  4/Z;\\\\n- both anticommutator-distance bounds;\\\\n- all seven bounds at scale `C * Real.sqrt \\\\u03b5`.\\\\n\\\\n### Dependencies\\\\n\\\\n- Base on merged #75.\\\\n- Base on #49 for the clean state-dependent distance/observable conversion and\\\\n  triangle API, especially `opFamilyDistSq_le_of_le_of_le`,\\\\n  `consistencyDefect_postprocess_le`, and `povm_to_obs` where applicable.\\\\n- Base on #64 for clean EPR normalization and the Pauli-projector/observable\\\\n  expansions used to identify `idealMagicBitProj`.\\\\n- Base on #68 for the binary Pauli involution and twisted-commutation laws.\\\\n- It is independent of the perfect-strategy packet, #69, the fixed-field-model\\\\n  work, and encoding/decoding. Once the split and these three dependencies\\\\n  land, rigidity and perfect strategy may run concurrently in disjoint files.\\\\n\\\\n### Proof route\\\\n\\\\n1. Expand the game value over the 36 directed constraint-variable incidences.\\\\n   Convert `1 - \\\\u03b5 \\\\u2264 S.value` into rejection-mass bounds, then into the\\\\n   finitely many row/column consistency relations with explicit constants.\\\\n   Include bounds for wrong-form answers folded by `msBitOrZero`; they are not\\\\n   definitionally absent.\\\\n2. Reduce arbitrary finite POVMs to projective measurements without\\\\n   strengthening the theorem. Reuse or adapt the proved one-measurement and\\\\n   tensor-product Naimark machinery in\\\\n   `MIPStarRE/LDT/MakingMeasurementsProjective/NaimarkFull.lean`, but prove the\\\\n   pure-vector/intertwining consequences actually needed here: value\\\\n   preservation, composition of the input-space embeddings with the eventual\\\\n   self-test isometries, and transfer of state-dependent effect bounds back to\\\\n   the original strategy.\\\\n3. For the dilated projective strategy, turn the six nearly satisfied parity\\\\n   constraints and same-cell agreement into approximate reflection relations.\\\\n   Isolate a proved, file-local projective Magic Square rigidity lemma;\\\\n   projectivity must be discharged by step 2, not exposed in\\\\n   `exists_ms_rigidity`.\\\\n4. Follow the finite Magic Square operator argument: extract approximate Pauli\\\\n   `X` and `Z` pairs for the two logical qubits, construct the local swap\\\\n   isometries, and obtain a normalized auxiliary vector. Keep all intermediate\\\\n   relation/error lemmas concrete and proved. Do not restate\\\\n   Coladangelo--Stark's general theorem as an axiom or assumed proposition.\\\\n5. Translate the cited theorem's ideal observables `I\\\\u2297Z` and `ZX\\\\u2297ZX` through\\\\n   the explicit local basis change to the project's `X\\\\u2297I` and `Z\\\\u2297I`. Use\\\\n   #64/#68 to identify the corresponding\\\\n   binary effects with `idealMagicBitProj`.\\\\n6. Convert the self-test's density/trace estimate to the exact Euclidean vector\\\\n   estimate. Account for the square-root loss explicitly; this is not a\\\\n   definitional `simpa`.\\\\n7. Derive the four `msOperatorDistanceA/B` bounds, then the two\\\\n   `msAnticommutatorDistanceA/B` bounds from binary observable expansion,\\\\n   multiplication stability, and the squared-distance triangle estimates from\\\\n   #49.\\\\n8. Track explicit constants throughout and take a finite maximum to obtain the\\\\n   single universal `C \\\\u2265 1`. Handle the theorem's unrestricted `\\\\u03b5 \\\\u2265 0`: use\\\\n   the robust argument in its small-error range and a separately\\\\n   proved coarse large-error bound with canonical padded isometries. Do not\\\\n   silently assume `\\\\u03b5 \\\\u2264 1`.\\\\n\\\\nPrivate implementation submodules under\\\\n`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems/Rigidity/` are allowed when they keep\\\\nindividual proofs reviewable. They remain owned by this one issue and must\\\\nbottom out in Lean/Mathlib and the already proved local APIs.\\\\n\\\\n### Statement integrity\\\\n\\\\nPaper assumptions: an arbitrary finite-dimensional strategy whose Magic Square\\\\nsuccess is `1-\\\\u03b5`. Lean uses arbitrary finite local carriers, a unit pure state,\\\\narbitrary POVMs, nonnegative `\\\\u03b5`, and a lower success bound; the\\\\nlower-bound form is the faithful monotone version of the source equality.\\\\nPaper conclusion: local isometries extracting two EPR pairs and an auxiliary\\\\nstate, four binary measurement approximations, and Alice/Bob anticommutation,\\\\nall with universal `O(sqrt \\\\u03b5)` control. Lean records exactly these\\\\nthrough `MsRigidityWitness`, `idealMsState`, `msOperatorDistanceA/B`, and\\\\n`msAnticommutatorDistanceA/B`; indices 0 and 4 are the paper's variables 1 and\\\\n5. Verdict: faithful explicit-constant encoding.\\\\n\\\\nThe paper explains two translations at lines 650-652: trace norm to Euclidean\\\\ndistance and a local basis change. Both are proof obligations. No additional\\\\nstrategy-projectivity assumption, bridge package, residual input, or changed\\\\nerror exponent is source-faithful.\\\\n\\\\n### Ownership and non-goals\\\\n\\\\nOwn `MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems.lean` and, if needed, new private\\\\nrigidity-only submodules below\\\\n`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems/Rigidity/`. Do not touch\\\\n`MagicSquare.lean`, `MagicSquareTheorems/Basic.lean`,\\\\n`MagicSquareTheorems/PerfectStrategy.lean`, Pauli/distance source files,\\\\nblueprint, re-exports, or downstream soundness files.\\\\n\\\\nDo not add `S.IsProjective`, restrict the strategy dimension, drop either\\\\nplayer's conclusions, omit the wrong-form answer analysis, move `C` under\\\\n`\\\\u03b5` or `S`, replace `sqrt \\\\u03b5` by a weaker rate, add an\\\\nexternal-theorem axiom, leave a conditional self-test helper, or create a\\\\ngeneral LCS/group-stability framework. Do not add new issues merely for\\\\nmechanisms discovered during proof work; keep necessary private lemmas in this\\\\npacket.\\\\n\\\\n### Acceptance\\\\n\\\\n- `exists_ms_rigidity` is complete with its exact existing signature and all\\\\n  seven bounds.\\\\n- Every helper on its proof path is kernel-checked; its `#print axioms` output\\\\n  contains no `sorryAx` or new axiom.\\\\n- The owned file/submodules contain no `sorry`, `admit`, prohibited bypass,\\\\n  conditional bridge, or `**Unfaithful:**` dependency.\\\\n- The statement-integrity audit explicitly records POVM generality, quantifier\\\\n  order, zero-based indices, the universal constant, trace-to-Euclidean\\\\n  conversion, local basis change, and the large-error branch.\\\\n- Focused rigidity modules and `MIPStarRE/QPBT.lean` type-check; full build,\\\\n  declaration check, blueprint render/status checks, diff check, exact-head CI,\\\\n  and independent review pass.\\\\n- Existing blueprint declaration links remain unchanged; no new `\\\\\\\\leanok` claim\\\\n  is added.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\nStage 4.3 proof packet under #47.\\\\n\\\",\\n./results/telemetry/github-snapshot/open-issues.json:3351:  \\\"body\\\": \\\"<!-- mipstarre-issue-key: qpbt-stage43-magic-square-perfect-strategy -->\\\\n### Motivation\\\\n\\\\nProve the converse Magic Square construction `thm:ms-from-ac`: any exact\\\\nanticommuting pair of consistent binary projective measurements extends to a\\\\nvalue-one SPCC Magic Square strategy. The canonical statement and full\\\\noperator-table proof are\\\\n`references/qpbt-paper/08_classical_and_quantum_low_degree_tests.tex:654-878`;\\\\nthe matched blueprint node is\\\\n`blueprint/src/chapter/ch13_qpbt_test.tex:255-286`.\\\\n\\\\n### Target\\\\n\\\\nAfter the Magic Square foundation/split packet #75, prove only the existing\\\\ndeclaration `MIPStarRE.QPBT.exists_ms_perfect_strategy_of_anticommuting` in\\\\n`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems/PerfectStrategy.lean`, preserving its\\\\nsignature verbatim.\\\\n\\\\nIn particular preserve arbitrary finite nonempty `\\\\u03b9`, the hypotheses `hA`,\\\\n`hB`, `hcA`, `hcB`, and `hac`, and every exact conclusion: `S.\\\\u03b9 = \\\\u03b9 \\\\u00d7 ZMod 2`,\\\\n`S.IsSPCC`, value `1`, state `msPerfectState \\\\u03b9`, and the\\\\nvariable-0/variable-4 effect embeddings.\\\\n\\\\n### Dependencies\\\\n\\\\n- Base on merged #75.\\\\n- Base on #64 for the clean `eprState_norm` theorem used to normalize\\\\n  `msPerfectState`.\\\\n- This packet is independent of #49, #68, the rigidity packet, #69, and\\\\n  encoding/decoding. If #68 is already merged, reuse a directly applicable\\\\n  binary identity only when it avoids local duplication; do not make it a hard\\\\n  dependency or introduce type-reindexing infrastructure merely to use it.\\\\n\\\\n### Proof route\\\\n\\\\n1. From `hA` and `hB`, establish locally that `obsOf A` and `obsOf B` are\\\\n   Hermitian involutions and recover each binary effect as\\\\n   `(1 \\\\u00b1 obsOf _)/2`.\\\\n2. Define the single-qubit `X` and `Z` observables on `ZMod 2` from the existing\\\\n   concrete Pauli matrices, or equivalent private entrywise definitions. Prove\\\\n   their Hermiticity, involution, exact anticommutation, and consistency on\\\\n   `eprState (ZMod 2)` by finite extensional calculation.\\\\n3. Define the nine cell observables exactly as the paper's table:\\\\n\\\\n   `OA\\\\u2297I, I\\\\u2297X, OA\\\\u2297X; I\\\\u2297Z, OB\\\\u2297I, OB\\\\u2297Z; OA\\\\u2297Z, OB\\\\u2297X, OA*OB\\\\u2297Z*X`.\\\\n\\\\n4. Use `hac` and `XZ = -ZX` to prove that the bottom-right cell is Hermitian\\\\n   and squares to one. Prove pairwise commutation within all six rows/columns,\\\\n   and that their products are `I` except for the final column, whose product\\\\n   is `-I`.\\\\n5. Turn each Hermitian involution into its binary PVM. For variable questions,\\\\n   embed `.bit b` and assign zero to `.triple _`.\\\\n6. For each constraint, define the joint triple PVM by multiplying the three\\\\n   commuting cell projections. Embed `.triple beta` and assign zero to `.bit\\\\n   _`; prove positivity, completeness, orthogonality, and idempotence from\\\\n   pairwise commutation.\\\\n7. Assemble the symmetric strategy on local carrier `\\\\u03b9 \\\\u00d7 ZMod 2`, so the\\\\n   equality witness is `rfl`; normalize and swap the state `reindexState\\\\n   prodShuffle (vecTensor (eprState \\\\u03b9) (eprState (ZMod 2)))` using #64 and\\\\n   tensor/reindex norm laws.\\\\n8. Prove SPCC in order: projectivity for both question forms, cell/constraint\\\\n   consistency on the tensor EPR state, then support-wise commutation for each\\\\n   constraint-variable incidence.\\\\n9. Prove value one supportwise: parity follows from the six row/column product\\\\n   identities and answer consistency follows from the joint measurement\\\\n   marginal. Sum accepted outcomes to one using measurement completeness and\\\\n   `msGame.\\\\u03bc_prob`.\\\\n10. Finish the exact variable-0 and variable-4 effect equalities by unfolding\\\\n    the construction; do not replace them with observable-only equalities.\\\\n\\\\nKeep all operator-table, reflection-to-PVM, and finite-index lemmas private or\\\\nfile-local.\\\\n\\\\n### Statement integrity\\\\n\\\\nPaper assumptions: two binary PVMs on `(\\\\u2102^q)^{\\\\u2297n}`, EPR consistency, and\\\\nexact observable anticommutation. Lean assumptions: the same conditions on an\\\\narbitrary finite nonempty local carrier `\\\\u03b9`; `Fintype`, `DecidableEq`, and\\\\n`Nonempty` are representation boundary hypotheses. Paper conclusion: symmetric\\\\nvalue-one SPCC strategy on the original EPR system tensored with one EPR pair,\\\\nembedding `A` at variable 1 and `B` at variable 5. Lean conclusion is identical\\\\nafter zero-based labels 0 and 4 and explicit type transport `h\\\\u03b9`. Verdict:\\\\nfaithful carrier-generalized encoding, no extra load-bearing assumption and no\\\\nweakened conclusion.\\\\n\\\\n### Ownership and non-goals\\\\n\\\\nOwn only\\\\n`MIPStarRE/QPBT/Test/MagicSquareTheorems/PerfectStrategy.lean` after the split.\\\\nDo not touch `MagicSquare.lean`, `MagicSquareTheorems.lean` (the rigidity\\\\nowner/facade), its `Basic.lean`, Pauli or distance files, blueprint, re-exports,\\\\nor `Completeness.lean`.\\\\n\\\\nDo not change the theorem signature, restrict `\\\\u03b9` to a field model, weaken\\\\n`IsSPCC`, value, state, or effect equalities, postulate a joint-measurement API,\\\\nor add public mechanisms, bridge assumptions, conditional helpers, axioms, or\\\\nnew proof holes.\\\\n\\\\n### Acceptance\\\\n\\\\n- `exists_ms_perfect_strategy_of_anticommuting` is complete with its exact\\\\n  existing signature.\\\\n- Its `#print axioms` output contains no `sorryAx`.\\\\n- The owned file contains no `sorry`, `admit`, axiom, or prohibited bypass.\\\\n- The statement-integrity audit records the zero-based indices, carrier\\\\n  generalization, and exact state/effect conclusions.\\\\n- The focused file, `Test/Completeness.lean`, and `MIPStarRE/QPBT.lean`\\\\n  type-check; full build, declaration/blueprint checks, diff check, exact-head\\\\n  CI, and independent review pass.\\\\n- No blueprint or re-export edit is needed.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\nStage 4.3 proof packet under #47.\\\\n\\\",\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/bdca920242caf1f777bb40cb9a8117b7219a4a7b-code.md:44:(`references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020-1034`).\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/4277943db23d2dde26e90908ede8041fb7902e36-code.md:47:**F5–F6.** The divisibility note currently treats removal of the seed as the only game-format mismatch. Its directly indexed game still reveals an index and asks for a polynomial, unlike the cited pair measurement, and its verdict therefore overstates the proposed repair. Moreover, averaging each prover’s line measurement separately changes a seeded synchronicity correlation `E_s⟨M_s⊗N_s⟩` into `E_{s,s'}⟨M_s⊗N_{s'}⟩`; Naimark dilation preserves the latter, not the former. The note must give a faithful source comparison and a transport that actually controls all cross and synchronicity branches.\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/4277943db23d2dde26e90908ede8041fb7902e36-code.md:49:**F7.** `rem:qld-4-13-source-defects` correctly observes that the source statement at [14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/references/qpbt-paper/14_analysis_of_the_pauli_basis_test.tex:1020), label `lem:qld-4-13`, claims `poly(m²ε,md/q)`, while lines 1134–1137 prove only `m·poly(ε,md/q)` and lines 1241–1245 use an unsupported joint-law decomposition. Under [policy.tex](/Users/dengnifer/Documents/ghz/ldt/MIPStarRE-dev/.worktrees/issue-0002-qpbt-blueprint/docs/paper-gaps/policy.tex:19), lines 19–33 and 121–129, this requires a separate self-contained note and citation.\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/cf4cfa6eb26ad593c4e130d033b54e6a455a1ae1-code.md:26:- [-] F2 (blocker) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch15_qpbt_combining.tex:102` — `thm:linearity` strengthens the cited averaged rounding guarantee to pointwise closeness.  <!-- outdated at 39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785 -->\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785-prose.md:33:- [ ] F9 (changes) `blueprint/src/chapter/ch12_qpbt_games.tex:117` — The symmetrization proof uses the completed Naimark construction without listing its remark in `\\\\uses`.\\n./results/telemetry/registry-archive/prs/0001-docs-blueprint-qpbt-chapters-and-dependency-graph/reviews/39753e7304367b108d60e2a886fbb4349e0fc785-prose.md:46:For F4, move the convolution identity and projectivity at lines 823-835 into a lemma with a proof. Apply the same repair to the degree-support and projectivity assertions at lines 1025-1031. Definitions should introduce the operator families; derived properties belong in theorem or lemma nodes.\\n./MIPStarRE/LDT/ExpansionHypercubeGraph/MatrixRealization/Core.lean:573:Paper origin: `references/ldt-paper/expansion.tex:102-109`.\\n./MIPStarRE/LDT/ExpansionHypercubeGraph/MatrixRealization/Core.lean:795:Paper origin: `references/ldt-paper/expansion.tex:102-109`.\\n./MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionStep/Defs.lean:470:    (Real.rpow eps (1 / (1024 : Error)) +\\n./MIPStarRE/LDT/MainInductionSt